.TH CUMCAMS-DL 1 "2026-11-13" "cumcams-dl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cumcams-dl \- download cumcams.cc videos over HLS, queueing several at once
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cumcams-dl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIURL\fR
[\fIURL\fR...]
.P
.B cumcams-dl
\fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
[\fB\-P\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cumcams-dl
downloads archived shows from
.BR cumcams.cc ,
which exposes only an HLS
.I index.m3u8
playlist rather than a progressive file.
A two hour recording is roughly 3900 two-second segments.
.P
The tool walks the same anonymous chain the web player uses: the video page
supplies a
.I mid
cookie plus
.IR data-video-id " and " data-token ,
.B GET /api/video/\fIID\fB?token=\fI...
returns the player HTML, and that HTML contains a signed
.I index.m3u8
URL.
No account, cookie file, or clearance token is required.
.P
Segments are fetched in chunks with
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
and the finished chunks are concatenated and remuxed to Matroska by
.BR ffmpeg (1)
without re-encoding.
Throughput is capped at about 2 MB/s per video, so a two hour recording takes
somewhere near twenty minutes per video and videos downloaded together run in
parallel rather than competing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE"
Read URLs from
.IR FILE ,
one per line. Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored. Duplicates against the positional URLs are dropped.
.TP
.BI \-P " N"
Download
.I N
videos at once. Default:
.BR 2 .
This is the main throughput lever: the 2 MB/s ceiling applies per video, so
two videos roughly double the aggregate rate (measured 3.47 MB/s across two,
against 2.05 MB/s for one). Values above three are untested.
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory for finished files. Default:
.IR ~/Videos/cumcams .
.TP
.BI \-n " NAME"
Output basename, without extension. Only valid with a single URL; with several
names are derived from each stream path, e.g.\&
.IR nana_stolass_2026-09-29_13-16 .
.TP
.BI \-j " N"
Concurrent fragments per video, passed to
.BR yt\-dlp " \-N" .
Default:
.BR 2 .
This does little: runs at
.BR \-N " 1, 2 and 4"
all measured about 2.05 MB/s per video. Raising it only increases the chance
of tripping the connection shield described under
.BR BEHAVIOUR .
.TP
.BI \-\-nodes " N"
Edge nodes to spread each video across. Default:
.BR 1 ,
which is correct for this CDN. Raising it only helps during the short burst
allowance that follows an idle period.
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk\-size " N"
Segments per chunk. Default:
.BR 100 ,
about three and a half minutes of video. Keep this small: the connection
shield can cut a transfer at any moment, and this is the amount of work a
single cut throws away.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-segments " N"
Download only the first
.I N
segments of each video. Default
.B 0
means the whole stream. Useful for a smoke test.
.TP
.BI \-\-attempts " N"
Attempts per chunk before giving up. Default:
.BR 6 .
Rate-limit and connection failures back off progressively, up to ten minutes
per wait; a deterministic failure such as a malformed URL aborts immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-split
Use a single edge node and a single worker.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-chunks
Keep the per-chunk
.I .ts
files after the concatenation succeeds.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mux
Download only. Leave the per-chunk
.I .ts
files in the work directory and skip the
.BR ffmpeg (1)
concat and remux.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print each resolved stream URL and page title.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS The 2 MB/s ceiling, and why a browser is unaffected
Sustained download throughput is capped at roughly 2 MB/s
.B per video
and is flat within a video: one, two and four concurrent fragments all
measured about 2.05 MB/s.
Two separate videos measured 3.47 MB/s combined, and two processes pulling the
same video split the same 2 MB/s between them, so the budget follows the
stream rather than the socket.
.P
Short bursts are faster than the sustained rate, which is why a single
segment can appear to arrive at 5 MB/s while a long run settles at 2.
.P
The same CDN drops
.I new
TCP connection attempts for tens of seconds once too many are opened in a
short window; the client sees this as
.IR "No route to host" .
Connections that are already established are not affected.
This is why the web player keeps working while a downloader stalls: playback
needs about 1 MB/s against a 2 MB/s allowance, and the player holds one
long-lived connection instead of opening a fresh one per segment.
The shield is global to the client IP, so it applies across all videos at
once; it is the per-video budget, not the shield, that makes queueing pay.
.SS Queueing
Every URL given on the command line, plus every URL in the
.B \-\-file
list, is a job.
Up to
.B \-\-parallel
jobs run at the same time, each in its own thread with its own
.BR yt\-dlp
process, its own work directory, and its own 2 MB/s budget.
A failed video does not stop the others; the exit status reports the failure
and re-running the same command resumes only the missing chunks.
.SS Resume
Chunks are named
.IR NAME .0000.ts ,
.IR NAME .0001.ts ,
and so on, inside
.IR ${TMPDIR}/cumcams-dl-\fIID\fR .
A chunk that is already complete is skipped, so re-running the same command
continues where the previous run stopped, for every video in the queue.
Work directories are removed once the remux succeeds unless
.B \-\-keep\-chunks
or
.B \-\-no\-mux
is given.
.SS Edge node discovery
The API returns one edge host such as
.I vi5b.cdnhlscloud.com
on
.IR 92.246.93.20 .
When
.B \-\-nodes
is greater than one,
.B cumcams-dl
probes sibling letters under the same prefix and keeps the ones that answer
200, so
.I vi5a
on
.IR 92.246.93.19
is added when reachable.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR yt\-dlp
for the segment fetching.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR ffmpeg
unless
.B \-\-no\-mux
is used.
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.10 or newer with the
.I requests
module.
.SH EXAMPLES
Download a show with the defaults:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Queue two shows, two at a time:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200031521/play
.EE
.P
Queue everything in a list file, three at a time:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-f ~/cams-todo.txt \-P 3
.EE
.P
Send a single show somewhere else under a chosen name:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-o ~/Videos/cams \-n nana-2026-09-29 \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play
.EE
.P
Pull the first minute of each video, to check that the chain works:
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-\-max\-segments 30 \-\-chunk\-size 30 \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200367738/play \e
    https://cumcams.cc/video/200031521/play
.EE
.P
Recover from a CDN rate-limit: wait a few minutes, then re-run the identical
command. Completed chunks are skipped.
.IP
.EX
cumcams-dl \-f ~/cams-todo.txt
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success: every queue entry produced a file, or
.B \-\-no\-mux
left its chunks in place.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: bad arguments, a dependency is missing, the page or API layout
changed, the playlist is encrypted, or at least one video exhausted its
attempts.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with SIGINT. Re-running the same command resumes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Videos/cumcams
Default output directory.
.TP
.I ${TMPDIR}/cumcams-dl-\fIID\fR
Per-video work directory holding chunk playlists and intermediate
.I .ts
files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH BUGS
The per-video 2 MB/s ceiling cannot be raised by any client setting; only
downloading more videos at once increases the aggregate.
The connection shield is global to the client IP, so more parallel videos also
mean more new connections, and enough of them will stall the whole queue for
tens of seconds.
Chunk-level resume is coarse: a chunk interrupted halfway is re-fetched from
its first segment.
Widevine or SAMPLE-AES protected playlists are refused rather than handled.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
